{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4534","id":4734305455,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGi_Erw","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4534","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4534.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4534.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4534","number":4534,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29: preserve deadline findings after swallowed cancellation","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.1\nRelated: #1143; follow-up to #4527.\n\n## Problem and behavior\nAn asynchronous adapter can catch local cancellation and return a controlled rejection before the parent watchdog wins the race. That could hide an actual case deadline overrun.\n\nThe worker now gives its local abort state and measured elapsed time precedence after target execution, seed collection, and their exception paths. A late completion is a `case-timeout` finding, including synchronous work that delayed the abort callback. Normal bounded outcomes retain their classifications.\n\nThe finite cancellation-rejection probe has a fixed ID, runs through process isolation, and remains unavailable to ordinary campaigns. Existing process, memory, output, and corpus limits are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n- 21 focused tests passed: worker deadline, lifecycle, corpus, and mutation/budget primitives.\n- Command: `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap tests/conformance/fuzz/worker-deadline.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/lifecycle.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/corpus.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/primitives.test.js`.\n- Local Node 24.19.0, Linux x64; tested local commit `5bfd3a953abef99a7fd2bede2778bb1d1fe25e3a`.\n- Published tree is byte-identical to tested tree `741d080e96bd62b0628d45dd3ea8090783c39cac`. GitHub-created commit metadata differs from the local commit.\n- Independent source review and whitespace check passed. Ordinary required core runs static/build checks; it is not Node test qualification.\n\nThis fixes harness correctness. It does not assert completion of the broader fuzzing or platform qualification acceptance criteria.","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:20:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T12:21:37Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T12:21:37Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T12:21:37Z","merge_commit_sha":"7b7ed128017b4b966dfa389ab6eedef46e863985","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12526353617,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU59Ms88AAAAC6qD80Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/labels/size/L","name":"size/L","color":"A14C05","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4534/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4534/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.